INSERT INTO company_dossiers (ticker,status,content_json,verified_by,verified_at,published_at,updated_at) VALUES ('AAON','published','{"ticker":"AAON","reviewed":"August 2, 2026","completeness":100,"newsroomUrl":"https://investors.aaon.com/news-events/news-releases","description":"AAON operates in industrials, focused on engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications.","lede":"AAON gives owners exposure to engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications. The central question is whether its competitive position and reinvestment can convert demand into durable per-share cash generation after the full cost of capital, execution, and industry risk.","sells":"AAON provides engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications to commercial, industrial, aerospace, government, infrastructure, transportation, and service customers. Owners should verify segment mix, customer concentration, contract terms, and geographic exposure in the latest Form 10-K and 10-Q.","revenueModel":"Equipment, component, project, service, aftermarket, maintenance, distribution, and long-term contract revenue; backlog and orders are not the same as collected cash.","opportunity":"Replacement demand, automation, electrification, infrastructure investment, aerospace activity, and an installed base can support volume and aftermarket growth. For AAON, the owner must test whether engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications can gain profitable share rather than treating addressable-market growth as company value by itself.","mustGoRight":"Backlog must convert on schedule, price and productivity must offset input costs, quality must remain high, and capital-intensive programs must earn acceptable returns.","editorNote":"This owner brief uses the issuer''s SEC filing history, earnings-related 8-K record, proxy disclosures, and official company materials as its evidence spine. Bull and bear points are hypotheses to verify against the latest reported segment, cash-flow, balance-sheet, and management-commentary evidence—not recommendations or price targets.","bullTitle":"What the filing and call evidence could support","bull":["AAON''s position in engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume.","Engineering qualifications, distribution, installed equipment, regulatory approvals, customer integration, and service capability can create durable positions.","Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together.","Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion."],"bearTitle":"What owners must be prepared to disprove","bear":["Demand for engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow.","Customer capital spending and large programs can shift abruptly.","Materials, skilled labor, supplier performance, warranty, or certification failures can disrupt delivery.","Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash."],"thesisBreaker":"The owner thesis breaks if AAON cannot defend its position in engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications and repeatedly fails to convert reported growth into resilient per-share free cash flow after required investment, balance-sheet obligations, and dilution.","financialDrivers":[{"label":"ORDERS & BACKLOG","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"book-to-bill, cancellations, program timing, price, mix, and conversion"},{"label":"AFTERMARKET & SERVICE","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"installed base, utilization, attach, pricing, maintenance, and recurring mix"},{"label":"MARGIN & CASH","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"volume, price-cost, productivity, working capital, capex, and free cash flow"},{"label":"REVENUE QUALITY","value":"Growth versus durability","detail":"Separate price, volume, mix, acquisitions, foreign exchange, backlog, and one-time items; reconcile growth with retention and cash collection."},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Resilience and optionality","detail":"Track cash, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, covenants, refinancing needs, and contingent liabilities disclosed in the latest filing."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner cash conversion","detail":"Reconcile net income with operating cash, capex, acquisitions, dividends, repurchases, stock compensation, and diluted share count."}],"risks":[{"title":"Cycle and project timing","level":"High","text":"Customer capital spending and large programs can shift abruptly.","signal":"Orders, backlog, cancellations, inventory, and utilization"},{"title":"Supply, labor, and quality","level":"High","text":"Materials, skilled labor, supplier performance, warranty, or certification failures can disrupt delivery.","signal":"Lead times, cost inflation, rework, and customer penalties"},{"title":"Contract and regulatory exposure","level":"High","text":"Fixed-price work, government rules, safety, and environmental obligations can impair economics.","signal":"Estimate-at-completion changes, claims, investigations, and remedies"},{"title":"Capital allocation","level":"Medium","text":"Acquisitions, internal investment, debt, dividends, and repurchases can create or destroy per-share value.","signal":"Return on invested capital, impairments, leverage, share count, and post-investment cash generation"},{"title":"Reporting, legal, and governance","level":"Medium","text":"Controls, estimates, litigation, tax, incentives, or governance choices can alter reported economics and owner outcomes.","signal":"Restatements, control weaknesses, estimate changes, proceedings, proxy incentives, and related-party disclosures"}],"monitor":[{"title":"Latest 10-Q versus prior expectations","text":"Compare reported operating drivers, cash conversion, balance-sheet changes, and risk language with the prior quarter and owner thesis.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Management commentary versus delivery","text":"Record the measurable commitments made in the latest official earnings materials and test them against subsequent filings.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Downside leading indicators","text":"Watch Orders, backlog, cancellations, inventory, and utilization; Lead times, cost inflation, rework, and customer penalties; Estimate-at-completion changes, claims, investigations, and remedies.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital allocation","text":"Measure whether retained cash, acquisitions, debt reduction, dividends, and repurchases improve durable value per diluted share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}],"questions":["Which disclosed operating metric best proves that AAON is strengthening its position in engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications?","What changed in the latest 10-Q relative to the preceding 10-K and management''s prior commentary?","Which portion of reported growth is recurring, contractual, or repeatable, and which portion is cyclical or one-time?","What balance-sheet or off-balance-sheet obligation matters most in a downside case?","Does management''s compensation framework reward per-share owner value or primarily scale and adjusted metrics?","What measurable development would invalidate the thesis rather than merely create short-term price volatility?"],"competitors":"AAON competes with public and private operators across engineered commercial HVAC equipment, controls, replacement parts, and high-efficiency cooling systems including data-center applications; the comparable set below is a research starting point and must be normalized for business mix, leverage, accounting, and capital intensity.","comparables":[{"name":"HONEYWELL INTERNATIONAL INC","ticker":"HON","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Industrials operating and valuation reference for AAON.","valuation":"Compare enterprise value, earnings, free cash flow, growth, capital intensity, and a sector-appropriate unit metric using current filings.","financialStatus":"Use the latest HON filing to compare profitability, liquidity, leverage, dilution, and cash conversion with AAON.","sourceUrl":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0000773840&owner=exclude"},{"name":"Eaton Corp plc","ticker":"ETN","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Industrials operating and valuation reference for AAON.","valuation":"Compare enterprise value, earnings, free cash flow, growth, capital intensity, and a sector-appropriate unit metric using current filings.","financialStatus":"Use the latest ETN filing to compare profitability, liquidity, leverage, dilution, and cash conversion with AAON.","sourceUrl":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001551182&owner=exclude"},{"name":"GENERAL ELECTRIC CO","ticker":"GE","ownership":"Public","relationship":"Industrials operating and valuation reference for AAON.","valuation":"Compare enterprise value, earnings, free cash flow, growth, capital intensity, and a sector-appropriate unit metric using current filings.","financialStatus":"Use the lates