VALUES ('AAMI','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for systematic investment strategies and research-driven asset management for institutional and intermediary clients can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Losses, volatility, collateral changes, or funding stress can impair capital. Capital rules, fiduciary duties, market structure, or misconduct can change economics. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','AAMI SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001748824&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides Acadian Asset Management''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
