VALUES ('AES','bull_case','editorial_analysis','AES CORP''s position in electric generation, regulated utilities, renewable energy, storage, long-term contracts, and grid modernization can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume. Exclusive service territories, irreplaceable networks, regulated cost recovery, generation assets, and long-lived customer relationships can support visibility. Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together. Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','AES official investor materials','https://www.aes.com/investors','Use the company''s official results, presentations, webcast replays, prepared remarks, and transcripts when the issuer makes them publicly available.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
