VALUES ('BNY','bull_case','editorial_analysis','BANK OF NEW YORK MELLON CORP''s position in asset servicing, custody, clearing, issuer services, treasury, wealth, and investment management can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume. Regulatory licenses, capital, liquidity, brand, distribution, data, switching costs, and network effects can create barriers to entry. Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together. Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','BNY official investor materials','https://www.bny.com/corporate/global/en/investor-relations.html','Use the company''s official results, presentations, webcast replays, prepared remarks, and transcripts when the issuer makes them publicly available.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
