VALUES ('BNY','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for asset servicing, custody, clearing, issuer services, treasury, wealth, and investment management can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Losses, volatility, collateral changes, or funding stress can impair capital. Capital rules, fiduciary duties, market structure, or misconduct can change economics. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','BNY SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001390777&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides BANK OF NEW YORK MELLON CORP''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
