VALUES ('CBRS','bull_case','editorial_analysis','Q1 2026 revenue increased 94% year over year to $193.4 million, with both hardware and cloud/services contributing. The OpenAI agreement commits 750 MW of inference capacity for expected deployment from 2026 through 2028 and includes an option for another 1.25 GW by 2030. Cerebras raised approximately $6.2 billion of net IPO proceeds, materially expanding the capital available for cloud deployment and product investment. Distribution through AWS Marketplace, Microsoft Marketplace, IBM watsonx, Vercel, OpenRouter, and Hugging Face can broaden access beyond direct system buyers.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','Cerebras IPO Closing','https://investors.cerebras.ai/news-releases/news-release-details/cerebras-systems-announces-closing-initial-public-offering','Cerebras sold 34.5 million Class A shares at $185 per share for approximately $6.38 billion of gross proceeds.','2026-08-03','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
