VALUES ('CBRS','bear_case','editorial_analysis','MBZUAI generated 63% and G42 11% of Q1 2026 revenue; three customers represented 86% of accounts receivable. Q1 property-and-equipment purchases were $132.0 million against $12.3 million of operating cash flow as Cerebras prepared a much larger cloud buildout. The company disclosed material weaknesses involving IT controls, segregation of duties, and accounting and finance staffing. The OpenAI arrangement carries deployment, performance, financing, and counterparty obligations; a large headline contract is not equivalent to earned revenue or free cash flow.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','Cerebras Q1 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2021728/000162828026044981/cbrs-20260331.htm','The first public quarterly filing reports revenue by type, margin, loss, cash flow, balance-sheet facts, customer concentration, OpenAI and AWS arrangements, controls, commitments, and risks.','2026-06-12','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
