VALUES ('CBRS','thesis_breaker','editorial_analysis','The thesis breaks if wafer-scale performance does not translate into repeatable customer economics, committed capacity is delayed or underutilized, or concentration and infrastructure obligations prevent revenue growth from producing durable per-share cash returns.','Defines evidence that would invalidate the ownership thesis.','Cerebras Q1 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2021728/000162828026044981/cbrs-20260331.htm','The first public quarterly filing reports revenue by type, margin, loss, cash flow, balance-sheet facts, customer concentration, OpenAI and AWS arrangements, controls, commitments, and risks.','2026-06-12','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
