VALUES ('CCI','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for U.S. communications towers, small cells, fiber, long-term tenant leases, amendments, and wireless infrastructure can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Vacancy, churn, customer consolidation, or property obsolescence can reduce cash flow. Leverage and maturities expose owners to rates and capital-market availability. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','CCI SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001051470&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides CROWN CASTLE INC''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
